course: dictionary
lesson: 6937
title: One word, many pages
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word page has more than one meaning, so context tells you which one you need. In «Turn the page», it means one side of a sheet of paper in a book. In «web page», it means one screen of a website.
explain: Look at the words around it. «On page 12» points to a numbered side of a book, and «front page» is usually the first side of a newspaper. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Page can also be a verb. In the sentence «The nurse will page Dr Lee», to page someone means to call them, for example over a speaker. Long ago, a page was a boy who served a knight or a king, so a dictionary can help you find all the meanings.
fact: A page is one side of a sheet of paper in a book, a magazine or a notebook.
fact: A web page is one screen of a website.
fact: «Index» means the list of topics at the back of a non-fiction book, with page numbers.
fact: «A book used 552 digits» to number its pages, and page numbers are counting numbers in order.
fact: To page someone means to call them, for example over a speaker.
exercise: «Turn the page.» What does page mean here? | A boy who served a knight | *One side of a sheet of paper in a book | A web page on a website | To call someone over a speaker
exercise: «A website is a set of files … which shows them as a page.» What does page mean here? | One side of a sheet of paper | A boy who served a knight | *One screen of a website | To call someone
exercise: «The nurse will page Dr Lee.» What does page mean? | A screen on a website | A boy who served a knight | *To call someone over a speaker | One side of a sheet of paper
test: «On page 12» points to which kind of page? | A boy who served a knight | A web page | A call over a speaker | *A numbered side of a book
test: Which sentence uses page as a verb? | Each chapter has 20 pages. | Turn the page now. | *The nurse will page Dr Lee. | Open the web page.
exam: Which meaning fits «the page loaded in two seconds»? | A boy who served a knight | To call someone over a speaker | One side of a sheet of paper in a book | *One screen of a website
